{
  "dom_id": "step-q127873",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "A nonzero vector $\u27e80,\\,b,\\,c\u27e9$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot \u27e8-3,1,-2\u27e9=7.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$",
  "worked_solution": "We need a vector $v=\u27e8{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}\u27e9$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot \u27e8-3,1,-2\u27e9=7$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=\u27e8-3,1,-2\u27e9.$ So, $v\u22a5n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ \u27e8{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8-3,1,-2\u27e9 & =0 \\\\ -3{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=\u27e8{t}_{1},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}\u27e9,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\u27e80,\\,2,\\,1\u27e9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$",
